# Project One Get-Item Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: get-item and inventory design for M7 Project Two
#
# Review the course-provided get-item flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, SET, ADD, or similar terms.

# TODO 1: Identify the information the get-item process needs.
# Consider the current room, item in that room, and player's inventory.
SET current_room TO "Living room"
SET player_inventory TO empty list
SET item_input TO ""

# TODO 2: Prompt for and receive the player's get-item command.
OUTPUT "You are in the " + current_room
OUTPUT "Enter a command (e.g., 'get <item_name>'): "
INPUT item_input

# TODO 3: Validate whether the requested item is available in the current
# room. Show the decision clearly.
Mapping items to rooms based on storyboard:
# Towel closet -> "Kitchen towels"
# Bathroom -> "Mop"
# Cleaning closet -> "Cleaning spray"
# Bedroom -> "Broom"
# Laundry room -> "Scrub daddy"
# Pantry closet -> "Flour"

SET room_item TO "None"

IF current_room EQUALS "Towel closet" THEN
    SET room_item TO "Kitchen towels"
ELSE IF current_room EQUALS "Bathroom" THEN
    SET room_item TO "Mop"
ELSE IF current_room EQUALS "Cleaning closet" THEN
    SET room_item TO "Cleaning spray"
ELSE IF current_room EQUALS "Bedroom" THEN
    SET room_item TO "Broom"
ELSE IF current_room EQUALS "Laundry room" THEN
    SET room_item TO "Scrub daddy"
ELSE IF current_room EQUALS "Pantry closet" THEN
    SET room_item TO "Flour"

IF item_input MATCHES room_item AND room_item NOT EQUAL TO "None" THEN
    SET is_valid_item TO TRUE
ELSE
    SET is_valid_item TO FALSE
ENDIF
TODO 4: Describe what happens when the item request is valid.
# Include the inventory update and player output.
IF is_valid_item EQUALS TRUE THEN
    ADD room_item TO player_inventory
    OUTPUT "You picked up the " + room_item + "!"
    SET room_item TO "None"

# TODO 5: Describe what happens when the item request is invalid.
# Include the output the player should receive.
IF is_valid_item EQUALS FALSE THEN
    OUTPUT "That item is not in this room, or you entered an invalid command."

# TODO 6: Show how the process returns to or continues the larger gameplay
# loop after the command is handled.
WHILE game is running DO
    CALL prompt for item command (TODO 2)
    CALL validate item (TODO 3)
    IF valid THEN add to inventory (TODO 4) ELSE display error (TODO 5)
